#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:86 c21f3ea9ff4a4524b7f23f87bdee0bc8
msgid "Episodes: terminated vs truncated"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:88 a0e051248f3d40c687bb53a183ba2621
msgid "The Gymnasium convention is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:90 c79e26b7d2ed40ad9ca1109c943d157e
msgid ""
"**`terminated`**: the episode reached a *natural* end (won, lost, or ran "
"out of valid states)."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:92 65f20a7905cc49d4bc02d037a5a5a5bc
msgid "**`truncated`**: the episode was *cut* by an artificial time limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:94 1c95fb5bface42f4ae7f1af1b6916d1b
msgid "In `TradingEnv`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:96 f2c901fa80844088a05d5b6276eef7d9
msgid ""
"`terminated` fires when there's no more data (`current_step == len(data) "
"- 1`). The episode is \"complete.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:98 7770aa5ba828480d95690db3385c4d3d
msgid ""
"`truncated` fires when `max_steps` is reached. The episode could have "
"continued but you set a budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:101 5c053610252c4efcbd52a2ff77155d94
msgid ""
"`stable-baselines3`'s value bootstrapping treats them differently — make "
"sure you set `max_steps` short enough that most episodes truncate (so the"
" agent learns from many short episodes), but not so short that the "
"strategy never has time to play out."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:106 c5e963418aef4aa3bbc07e37f9562618
msgid "`random_start` for episode diversity"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:108 849690a069a74283abc220c3797e8ab5
msgid ""
"By default `random_start=False`: every episode starts at bar index "
"`window_size`. With `random_start=True`, each `reset()` picks a random "
"start in `[window_size, len(data) - max_steps)`, so episodes sample "
"different market regimes."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/trading_environment.md:113 f7e9967be0dd4c9290afabc341933eb9
msgid ""
"Required: `len(data) > window_size + max_steps`. The constructor raises a"
" clear `ValueError` if not — keep `max_steps` < `len(data) - window_size`"
" to leave room."
msgstr ""

